@id n2_choirc
# DRAFT
# Brother Piers on the east walk at dusk (night 2), watching the rain. Background.
# The drowned merchant (Thomas says drunk, so drunk it is), or the abbot's dreams and Bede off sulking.
== start
(Brother Piers on the east walk, watching the rain fill the garden beds.)
-> dead [if died_merchant]
-> plain

== dead
Piers {grave}: A man drowned in our fishpond. I'll not eat the carp this side of Easter.
-> topics

== plain
Piers {weary}: Rain again. The cloister drain's choked. It'll be over our shoes by Matins.
-> topics

== again
Piers {weary}: Still raining.
-> topics

== topics
* [if not n2_choirc_talk] What are the brothers saying? -> talk

== talk [set n2_choirc_talk]
-> talk_dead [if died_merchant]
-> talk_plain

== talk_dead
Piers {cold}: That Thomas says he drowned drunk, so he drowned drunk. (He doesn't smile.) Thomas is never wrong about the dead.
-> end

== talk_plain
Piers {weary}: That the abbot's dreaming badly, and Bede's gone off sulking again. Nothing new.
-> end

== leave
Piers {calm}: Keep dry, porter.
